(supporting evidence from other sources.) Tj T*
(A first proposal) Tj T*
(So what would this "O*NET for AI R&D" actually look like? This is of course not trivial to) Tj T*
(answer  -  AI R&D is very messy and changes fast. But we figured we'd have an initial attempt) Tj T*
(at it and let you readers bombard us with feedback. To that end, we compiled over sixty) Tj T*
(representative tasks at frontier AI labs, accompanied by descriptions and concrete examples  -) Tj T*
(see the full writeup here.) Tj T*
(The first step was to make a big list of all the tasks currently involved in AI R&D, which we) Tj T*
(grouped into six categories, inspired by some earlier work.2 These categories correspond to) Tj T*
(different parts of the AI research cycle:) Tj T*
(Each category has its own inputs and outputs. For example, consider Category 4 \("Run"\), which) Tj T*
(as the name suggests is about "running" stuff  -  think executing training runs or deploying AI) Tj T*
(systems to the public. So the input could look something like a benchmark with all supporting) Tj T*
(scaffolds and related infrastructure, and the output could be a set of final results.) Tj T*
(Each category is then split into several subcategories. Category 4 is split into three, each) Tj T*
(with its own inputs and outputs:) Tj T*
(4.1 Monitoring runs: watch training, RL, and eval runs in flight; catch problems as they) Tj T*
(emerge; restore the run to a healthy trajectory) Tj T*
(4.2 Hardware infrastructure operations: keep large clusters healthy, well-utilized, and quickly) Tj T*
(recoverable) Tj T*
(4.3 Inference reliability engineering: keep production serving stable, performant, and) Tj T*
(recoverable) Tj T*
(And finally the subcategories contain a thorough list of different tasks. For example, here are) Tj T*
(the tasks for "4.1 Monitoring runs":) Tj T*
(So you can see that this is way more granular than developing "solutions involving computer) Tj T*
(hardware and software"  -  our task descriptions get to the level of monitoring runs, and) Tj T*
(catching potential issues when they arise.) Tj T*
(One thing you'll notice about each task is that it includes a number next to it  -  that) Tj T*
(reflects our initial approach to estimating automation impact across tasks. Specifically, we) Tj T*
(rate how much we think current AIs automate each task on a scale of 0 to 5, based on the) Tj T*
(following rubric:) Tj T*
(RatingAI's automation0Not used, AI adds nothing1Marginal, occasionally convenient for lookups,) Tj T*
(brainstorming, or polishing writeups, but doesn't change how the work is done or who is doing) Tj T*
(it2Assists, with meaningful speed ups or improvements to parts of the task; human mostly drives) Tj T*
(and reviews everything3Collaborates, with AI doing large chunks under close human direction;) Tj T*
(human still makes calls and stitches things together4Leads, completing most of the task end to) Tj T*
(end from a high-level ask; human supervises, course-corrects, and approves outputs.5Autonomous,) Tj T*
(end to end with little or no human involvement) Tj T*
(We provide examples of each of these in the full proposal.) Tj T*
(This is of course quite subjective and there's a ton of room for people to develop better ways) Tj T*
(to evaluate this, such as through internal benchmarks. Optimistically, an improved version of) Tj T*
(this could be used to construct a metric that we can extrapolate over time. This could be quite) Tj T*
(tricky, because we'd need to know which tasks need to be automated to kick off an intelligence) Tj T*
(explosion, and there might be new tasks. For example, perhaps AIs don't need to "write a memo) Tj T*
(summarizing key takeaways" \(unlike human researchers\), if they have other ways of communicating) Tj T*
(with other AIs.) Tj T*
(But our overall hope is simply that our full collection of tasks gives us an additional signal) Tj T*
(about what AI can and can't automate at any point in time, supporting existing evidence we have) Tj T*
(from benchmarks and things like METR's time horizons.) Tj T*
(What's next?) Tj T*
(It goes without saying, but just to be excessively clear, this was an initial attempt at an) Tj T*
(O*NET for AI research. The most natural next step is to build on what's here and add tasks we) Tj T*
ET
endstream
