BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 54 738 Td
(missed, sharpen descriptions to be more precise and accurate, taxonomize to be more mutually) Tj T*
(exclusive and collectively exhaustive, and re-rate the list as AI improves.) Tj T*
(A step further would be to find other ways of organizing the taxonomy. For example, we thought) Tj T*
(about organizing all the tasks around the usual stages of model development, namely pre-) Tj T*
(training, post-training, and inference. We opted against it because it runs into several) Tj T*
(problems: \(1\) many tasks like "writing code for experiments" would be repeated across multiple) Tj T*
(stages, and \(2\) some tasks won't fit naturally in these categories, not least because the) Tj T*
(training process can look super complex in practice. But just because we decided against this) Tj T*
(categorization doesn't mean that it's not workable.) Tj T*
(Training isn't just a matter of "pre-training + post-training"  -  it's way more complicated) Tj T*
(than that.) Tj T*
(And we can say similar things about how we split up tasks: we'd ask if a task could be split) Tj T*
(into subtasks that would plausibly be automated at very different times  -  if we could, we'd) Tj T*
(split it up. We also tried to be more granular around tasks that require some amount of "taste") Tj T*
(\(such as whether to scale up a particular post-training recipe\), since people seem to disagree) Tj T*
(about this. But you could choose different levels of granularity for sure.) Tj T*
(In general, we'd be very excited about collaborating with people to improve on our initial) Tj T*
(attempt. If you're an AI researcher and think that we've messed up something in our) Tj T*
(classification or task descriptions, please share feedback or reach out! Or if you're somebody) Tj T*
(who'd use something like an O*NET for AI R&D in your work, we'd love to talk to you and) Tj T*
(understand how we can improve things to suit your needs.) Tj T*
(If this project goes well, we hope that it'll serve as a stepping stone toward more directly) Tj T*
(tracking AI R&D automation, helping AI forecasters extrapolate trendlines further forward  -) Tj T*
(and hopefully also tell us if the intelligence explosion is upon us.) Tj T*
(We'd like to thank David Owen, Stefania Guerra, Robert Sandler, and Elliot Stewart for their) Tj T*
(feedback and support.) Tj T*
(Please also see our initial attempt and the accompanying feedback form. For direct corrections) Tj T*
(or specific inquiries, you can email js@epoch.ai.) Tj T*
(Notes) Tj T*
(Depending on how you define it, an intelligence explosion could "start" well before fully) Tj T*
(automating AI research, because AIs would likely provide substantial uplift prior to that.) Tj T*
(It's possible that future AI systems make progress through routes that just really do not) Tj T*
(resemble current human AI R&D. If so, a task list based on current human workflows would) Tj T*
(completely miss the action, and our ontology would need to be updated at the very least.) Tj T*
